      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the value of \\( b \\) such that the equations \\( 2x + 7 = 3 \\) and \\( bx - 10 = -2 \\) have the same solution \\( x \\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Solve the first equation for \\( x \\):**\n   \\[\n   2x + 7 = 3\n   \\]\n   Subtract 7 from both sides:\n   \\[\n   2x = 3 - 7\n   \\]\n   Simplify the right side:\n   \\[\n   2x = -4\n   \\]\n   Divide both sides by 2:\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{-4}{2} = -2\n   \\]\n\n2. **Substitute \\( x = -2 \\) into the second equation:**\n   \\[\n   bx - 10 = -2\n   \\]\n   Replace \\( x \\) with \\(-2\\):\n   \\[\n   b(-2) - 10 = -2\n   \\]\n   Simplify the left side:\n   \\[\n   -2b - 10 = -2\n   \\]\n   Add 10 to both sides:\n   \\[\n   -2b = -2 + 10\n   \\]\n   Simplify the right side:\n   \\[\n   -2b = 8\n   \\]\n   Divide both sides by \\(-2\\):\n   \\[\n   b = \\frac{8}{-2} = -4\n   \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( b \\) is \\(\\boxed{-4}\\).",
